* Hard-Clip Distortion — exported from Lutherie
* An op-amp gain stage (up to about 200×) followed by two germanium diodes to ground, which chop the signal off at ±0.3 V: the bright, raw hard clipping of the first op-amp distortion pedals of the 1970s.

Vsig SIGSRC 0 SIN(0 0.3 220.0) AC 1
Rsig SIGSRC IN 1k
CC1 IN N2 10n
RR1 N2 N3 10k
RR2 N3 VCC_4p5V 1Meg
XU1 N3 N5 N6 OPAMP_LM741_20_70
RR3 N5 N6 1Meg
RR4 N7 N5 4.7k
CC2 N8 N7 47n
* Gain pot 500k B taper at 75%
RVR1a 0 0 375k
RVR1b 0 N8 125k
CC3 N6 N9 1u
RR5 N9 N10 10k
DD1 N10 0 D_1N34Agermanium
DD2 0 N10 D_1N34Agermanium
CC4 N10 0 1n
* Level pot 100k A taper at 90%
RVR2a 0 OUT 64k
RVR2b OUT N10 36k
Rload OUT 0 1Meg
VVS1 VCC_4p5V_src 0 DC 4.5
RVS1s VCC_4p5V_src VCC_4p5V 0.01

.model D_1N34Agermanium D(Is=2.6e-06 N=1.6 Rs=7.0 Cjo=5e-13 M=0)
* Behavioural op-amp: gain, gain-bandwidth, slew rate and output swing
.subckt OPAMP_LM741_20_70 INP INN OUT
Bin 0 M I=0.015915494309189534*tanh(0.2*V(INP,INN)/0.015915494309189534)
R1 M 0 1Meg
C1 M 0 3.183098861837907e-08
* keeps the internal node inside the swing, so the amplifier recovers from clipping at once
Bcl M 0 I=(ln(1+exp(min(8.0*(V(M)-6.25),60)))-ln(1+exp(min(8.0*(-V(M)-6.25),60))))/8.0
* soft saturation x/(1+x^4)^(1/4), written without pwr() because simulators disagree on its sign
Bout X 0 V=4.5+V(M)/sqrt(sqrt(1+(V(M)/2.5)*(V(M)/2.5)*(V(M)/2.5)*(V(M)/2.5)))
Rout X OUT 75.0
.ends

.options reltol=1e-5 abstol=1e-13 vntol=1e-8 method=trap
.tran 1.3020833333333333e-06 0.3 0 1.3020833333333333e-06
.control
set wr_singlescale
set numdgt=12
run
wrdata hard_clip_distortion.ngspice.txt v(OUT)
.endc
.end